  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Chlorine undergoes disproportionation in alkaline medium as shown below :<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>aCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>bOH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>cClO</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>dCl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>eH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>c</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> in a balanced redox reaction are respectively :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
